<title>USA: Pluma Inc Q1 shr $0.15 vs $0.01.</title>
<headline>Pluma Inc Q1 shr $0.15 vs $0.01.</headline>
<dateline>EDEN, N.C. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Unaudited)</p>
<p>						    First Quarter Ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net sales					  $27,286   $21,932</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold				22,593    19,022</p>
<p> Gross profit					 4,693     2,910</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses			 2,774     2,025</p>
<p> Income from operations			   1,919	 885</p>
<p> Other expenses, net				  551	 761</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		     1,368	 124</p>
<p> Income taxes					   503	  46</p>
<p> Net income					     865	  78</p>
<p>Earnings per common share and common</p>
<p>equivalents -- primary and</p>
<p>   fully diluted					.15	 .01</p>
<p>Weighted average number of common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding				5,899     5,316</p>
<p>	    (In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: The 11 percent increase in weighted average shares outstanding was a result of the company's initial public offering completed on March 10.</p>
<p>Sales and margin improvements were attributed in part to an improved product mix, an increase in units sold, lower yarn costs and better operating efficiencies.</p>
